    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for the breakdown. Regarding the homogenization, if we use high-shear mixing to drive those droplet sizes down, are we more likely to see a more resilient interfacial film, or does the increased surface area just create more \"weak points\" where the acetic acid can attack the lecithin layer? I'm concerned that the very process meant to stabilize the emulsion might actually make it more susceptible to rapid breakdown if the surfactant coverage isn't instantaneous.",
